.TH TENSCONV 1 "31 October 2026" "tenskit @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tensconv \- copy tensors into another container
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY tensconv
.B \-o
.I out
.RB [ \-\-format
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-rename ]
.RB [ \-\-names\-only ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.RB [ \-\-force\-single\-file ]
.I source
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tensconv
reads one container and writes one container.
A directory is the safetensors weight set, the same rule as
.BR \%tenspile (1).
Shapes are stored outermost-first.
A GGUF
.I ne[]
axis is reversed on the way in and on the way out.
A tensor whose bytes change (a widened dtype or a value change) is held in
memory until the output is written.
A GGUF name of 64 bytes or more, or a rank outside 1 to 4, stops the write.
A rank-0 tensor is stored as
.I ne=[1]
and its shape is kept in the key
.IR <name>.orig_shape .
.PP
Metadata is carried over.
GGUF keys keep their types in GGUF and rawtensor output, and become
.I gguf.<key>
JSON envelopes in safetensors and ONNX, such as
.IR {"type":"UINT32","value":4096} .
Tokenizer arrays are left out of those string maps.
Converting back to GGUF restores those keys with their types.
Other string metadata becomes
.I <format>.metadata.<key>
in GGUF.
npy, npz, and PyTorch output have no metadata, and a warning says so.
.PP
A dtype is copied when the target has it.
BF16 widens to F32.
FP8 and FP4 types that fit in F16 widen to F16.
E8M0 widens to F32.
A type the target cannot store stops the command.
Narrowing is not done.
With
.B \-\-rename
into GGUF, unless
.BR \-\-names\-only ,
F16 and BF16 norms, biases, and other 1-D tensors are widened to F32,
as llama.cpp's converter writes them (GGUF-024, GGUF-029).
Quantized blocks are not written here.
.BR \%tensquant (1)
dequantizes them.
.PP
An existing output file is left in place unless
.B \-\-force
is set.
Warnings go to stderr.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIfile\fR"
Output path.
Required.
The container is taken from
.B \-\-format
or from the file name.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " name"
Container to write.
.TP
.B \-\-rename
Map names through the GGUF role table.
The architecture is
.I \%general.architecture
or
.I config.json
.IR \%architectures[0] .
Hyperparameters written into GGUF follow
.IR \%hf_config_to_gguf :
.I text_config
is merged over the root object first, then the first listed key that is present is used.
Each row is written only under the condition of llama.cpp's
.IR \%TextModel.set_gguf_parameters ,
which the rows transcribe.
A sibling
.I config.json
is read only for those keys.
Value changes run unless
.B \-\-names\-only
is set.
A converter record with
.I complete: true
applies its listed branch.
The expression text is not evaluated.
Any other expression stops the conversion and prints that expression.
LLaMA
.I q_proj
and
.I k_proj
rows are permuted when that converter has
.IR undo_permute .
Qwen3.5 applies the V-head reorder,
.I A_log
as
.IR \-exp ,
norms other than
.I \%linear_attn.norm.weight
as
.IR "weight + 1" ,
and the
.I conv1d
squeeze.
Full-attention Q and K are not permuted.
The reorder is skipped when the linear head counts match.
An architecture whose record is
.I complete: false
and that is not the LLaMA or Qwen3.5 case stops and names
.IR unexpanded .
A BF16 tensor is changed in F32, as llama.cpp's converter does (GGUF-036),
and returns to BF16 afterwards unless it is written as F32.
.TP
.B \-\-names\-only
Rename and skip the value changes.
Applies to
.BR \-\-rename .
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite an existing output file.
.TP
.BI \-\-force\-single\-file " path"
Read this
.I .safetensors
file even when
.I config.json
is in the same directory.
It applies only to the path written immediately after it.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the short help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The output file was written.
.TP
.B 1
An error.
The message is written to stderr and starts with
.BR "\%tensconv: " .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Convert safetensors to GGUF, keeping the names:
.RS
.EX
tensconv \-o model.gguf model.safetensors
.EE
.RE
.PP
Convert a Hugging Face directory to GGUF names, with its config.json hyperparameters:
.RS
.EX
tensconv \-\-rename \-o model.gguf model/
.EE
.RE
.PP
Show the name mapping without changing any values:
.RS
.EX
tensconv \-\-rename \-\-names\-only \-o names.gguf model/
.EE
.RE
.PP
Convert GGUF to NumPy or to a PyTorch state_dict:
.RS
.EX
tensconv \-o weights.npz model.gguf
tensconv \-o model.pt model.gguf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Name the output format when the file name does not:
.RS
.EX
tensconv \-\-format safetensors \-o pytorch_model.bin model.gguf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Check the result:
.RS
.EX
tensdiff model.safetensors model.gguf
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config.json
Beside the source file or in the source directory.
.B \-\-rename
reads the architecture and the hyperparameters from it.
.TP
.I generation_config.json
Beside
.IR config.json .
.B \-\-rename
into GGUF writes its sampler defaults as
.I \%general.sampling.*
(GGUF-038).
.SH AUTHOR
Nick Reynolds (goldnode)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR \%tenspile (1),
.BR \%tensinfo (1),
.BR tensdiff (1),
.BR \%tensquant (1)
